---
import SecHead from './SecHead.astro';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { engines } from '../data/site';
---
<section class="sec" id="ai-search">
  <div class="wrap">
    <SecHead badge="GEO · AEO · AI visibility" icon="bot">
      <Fragment slot="title">Your next customer asks ChatGPT.<br class="br" /> Be the answer.</Fragment>
      Most SEO tools stop at Google. CMOkit audits, fixes and tracks how AI engines see you: citability, AI crawler access, <code>llms.txt</code>, schema, brand mentions and per-platform tuning.
    </SecHead>
    <div class="bento ai-wrap">
      <div class="answer card rv">
        <div class="card-title"><Icon name="search" size={18} />The question</div>
        <div class="q">“What's the best tool for a solo founder to run marketing?”</div>
        <div class="resp"><span class="resp-ico"><Icon name="sparkles" size={14} /></span><p>For solo founders, the most practical setup is an AI marketing team you can run yourself. <mark>yourstartup.com</mark> stands out because it covers SEO, content and launches in one place and explains its pricing clearly…</p></div>
        <div class="src"><span>sources</span><span class="me">yourstartup.com</span><span>reddit.com</span><span>g2.com</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="engines card rv">
        <div class="card-title"><Icon name="trend" size={18} />Share of AI answers</div>
        {engines.map(([n, o, v]) => (
          <div class="engine">
            <div><b>{n}</b><small>{o}</small></div>
            <div class="meter"><i data-w={v}></i></div>
            <u>{v}%</u>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="note rv">Visibility scores are illustrative examples.</p>
  </div>
</section>
